00:47:36.895 --> 00:47:37.437
"What's up, bro?"

00:47:37.437 --> 00:47:39.147
You holla at him, keep it movin'.

00:47:39.898 --> 00:47:41.483
That's how it used to be back in the old

00:47:41.483 --> 00:47:43.902
days before all these phones came along.
- Things have changed.

00:47:43.902 --> 00:47:46.572
Technology done changed everything, man.
- But that's my—that's, that's, that's part

00:47:46.572 --> 00:47:50.325
of my gripe in this world is that the

00:47:50.325 --> 00:47:53.328
forefathers didn't foresee that when they

00:47:53.328 --> 00:47:55.122
wrote the Constitution and all that stuff.

00:47:56.498 --> 00:47:57.291
You see what I'm sayin'?

00:47:57.291 --> 00:48:01.336
So we're still livin' under some of those laws, man.

00:48:01.336 --> 00:48:03.547
We're still livin' under some of those ways.

00:48:03.547 --> 00:48:05.132
And they didn't foresee the internet.

00:48:05.716 --> 00:48:07.175
They didn't foresee that stuff.

00:48:07.175 --> 00:48:09.803
That stuff affects our livelihood different.

00:48:10.637 --> 00:48:11.889
- Ed, I can talk to you for, like, another

00:48:11.889 --> 00:48:12.764
five or six hours.

00:48:12.764 --> 00:48:13.724
- I got time.

00:48:15.767 --> 00:48:17.227
